{
    "screenId": "SimPanel",
    "boardId": "sunton-3248s035r",
    "panelWidth": 320,
    "panelHeight": 480,
    "rotation": 3,
    "theme": "dark",
    "comment": [
        "The design the simulator lays out and measures. Only the properties that differ from the catalogue's",
        "defaults are listed; tests/tools/designer-sim.js fills the rest in, so this stays readable.",
        "",
        "The geometry is chosen so that a mistake has somewhere to show: the band is flush to three edges, the",
        "title sits inside the band (the common 'label on a background' case, which means two widgets in",
        "overlapping cells), the button is at odd coordinates, the meter spans the full width, the two footer",
        "pieces share the vertical edge at x=240, and the spacer is a 3x3 flush against the right edge."
    ],
    "probe": {
        "comment": [
            "A spot to check paint rather than geometry. The button is probed because it is a widget whose",
            "background really is painted from its own property; the band cannot be, because the generator",
            "emits a theme-styled panel for a rect and ignores its fill. The point is left of centre so the",
            "button's centred text does not sit on it."
        ],
        "widget": "go",
        "x": 21,
        "y": 62
    },
    "widgets": [
        {
            "id": "band",
            "tag": "rect",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "width": 480,
            "height": 40,
            "props": {
                "fill": "#ff0000"
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "title",
            "tag": "label",
            "x": 17,
            "y": 3,
            "width": 200,
            "height": 24,
            "props": {
                "text": "Odd coordinates"
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "go",
            "tag": "button",
            "x": 17,
            "y": 48,
            "width": 43,
            "height": 29,
            "events": [
                "clicked"
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "knob",
            "tag": "circle",
            "x": 100,
            "y": 60,
            "width": 40,
            "height": 30
        },
        {
            "id": "meter",
            "tag": "progress",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 280,
            "width": 480,
            "height": 20,
            "props": {
                "value": 50
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "foot",
            "tag": "rect",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 300,
            "width": 240,
            "height": 20,
            "props": {
                "fill": "#102030"
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "foot2",
            "tag": "rect",
            "x": 240,
            "y": 300,
            "width": 240,
            "height": 20,
            "props": {
                "fill": "#203040"
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "tiny",
            "tag": "spacer",
            "x": 477,
            "y": 3,
            "width": 3,
            "height": 3
        },
        {
            "_comment": "Two more widgets that raise events, in the empty middle, so the event path can be driven.",
            "id": "eco",
            "tag": "toggle",
            "x": 60,
            "y": 120,
            "width": 40,
            "height": 30,
            "events": [
                "valueChanged"
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "ok",
            "tag": "button",
            "x": 300,
            "y": 120,
            "width": 60,
            "height": 30,
            "events": [
                "clicked"
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "fonted",
            "tag": "label",
            "x": 200,
            "y": 120,
            "width": 90,
            "height": 30,
            "props": {
                "text": "AB",
                "font": "test"
            }
        },
        {
            "_comment": "The same text set in one of the crate's own fonts. The markup has no attribute for those, so the emitter has to write a style expression -- and only a build can prove it is accepted and honoured.",
            "id": "builtin",
            "tag": "label",
            "x": 200,
            "y": 160,
            "width": 90,
            "height": 30,
            "props": {
                "text": "AB",
                "font": "Scaled6x10"
            }
        },
        {
            "_comment": "A button with a built-in font too: its font travels as a style expression starting from the button style, and this is what says whether the theme paints over it.",
            "id": "builtinButton",
            "tag": "button",
            "x": 300,
            "y": 160,
            "width": 90,
            "height": 30,
            "props": {
                "text": "AB",
                "font": "Vector(2)"
            },
            "events": [
                "clicked"
            ]
        }
    ],
    "empty": {
        "comment": "A point no widget covers, to check that a tap there raises nothing.",
        "x": 250,
        "y": 240
    },
    "fonts": [
        {
            "_comment": "A font the design declares, so the whole path -- declaration, reference, build-time BDF parse, render -- is exercised by every host check.",
            "id": "test",
            "src": "assets/test.bdf",
            "chars": "AB"
        }
    ]
}
